{"name":"Watermelon Pink","hex":"#c77690","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"watermelon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the species Citrullus lanatus, bearing a melon-like fruit.","The fruit of the watermelon plant, having a green rind and watery flesh that is typically bright red when ripe and contains black seeds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watermelon"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Watermelon","blocks":[{"text":"The watermelon is a species of flowering plant in the family Cucurbitaceae. It is a scrambling and trailing vine-like plant cultivated worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Taiwan_2009_Tainan_City_Organic_Farm_Watermelon_FRD_7962.jpg/330px-Taiwan_2009_Tainan_City_Organic_Farm_Watermelon_FRD_7962.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watermelon"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Watermelon_cross_BNC.jpg/500px-Watermelon_cross_BNC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp